1	// csrc/fused/sm_90/mega_mamba_real_adamw_tc.cu — R2 Mamba TENSOR-CORE cell driver
2	// TU (DESIGN-TC-PIPELINE.md Fork B, the Mamba counterpart of the decoder's
3	// mega_decoder_real_adamw_tc.cu). The bf16 wgmma fwd+bwd+AdamW persistent
4	// megakernel, compiled with -DSG_TUNED_GEMM_IMPL=1 so the wgmma branch of
5	// fused_mamba_megakernel.cuh is selected (the scalar default TU
6	// mega_mamba_real_adamw.cu is UNTOUCHED and ships as the live path).
7	//
8	// BUILD-ONLY second TU for the SAME (mamba × adamw) cell, selected by the GEMM
9	// impl token. It is NOT wired into compile.py / dispatch — the parity gate
10	// (tests/hw/test_mamba_tc.py) JIT-loads it via cpp_extension.load and drives it
11	// directly through the pybind entry below. setup.py AUTO-EXCLUDES it (it owns a
12	// PYBIND11_MODULE(TORCH_EXTENSION_NAME) → the content-based glob filter drops it).
13	//
14	// The pybind entry `tc_train_step` runs ONE Fork-B TC step over a flat fp32 param
15	// blob in place, returning (mean loss, reduced weight grad [total]) so the gate
16	// compares every grad per-tensor vs the bf16-rounded fp64 Mamba oracle (the
17	// keystone — the CPU mirror does NOT cover the tile-batched P1 + the TC dW).
18	//
19	// HONESTY: exercises the REAL tensor-core path (HGMMA in SASS). No scalar
20	// fallback for the 4 projections; the selective scan + conv1d stay scalar (the
21	// contract — REUSED verbatim from model_stage_mamba3.cuh, not re-implemented).
